{"name":"Amritsar","slug":"amritsar","state":"Punjab","tagline":"Golden City of Purity, Langar, and Baisakhi Feasts","description":"Home to the magnificent Golden Temple (Harmandir Sahib), echoing with divine Gurbani, selfless community Langar, and joyous Baisakhi fairs.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1514222134-b57cbb8ce073?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":31.634,"lng":74.8723},"culturalHighlights":["Baisakhi Mela","Guru Nanak Jayanti Prakash Parv","Diwali Bandi Chhor Divas"],"_id":"BNhElMxWjSqmJPdM"}
{"name":"Hyderabad","slug":"hyderabad","state":"Telangana","tagline":"City of Pearls, Charminar, and Bonalu Folk Splendor","description":"A blend of Nizami grandeur and vibrant Telugu folk traditions, celebrated through the sacred Bonalu Mahankali festival and Bathukamma floral feasts.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1605469237567-a39930679526?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":17.385,"lng":78.4867},"culturalHighlights":["Golconda & Lal Darwaza Bonalu","Bathukamma Floral Celebrations","Numaish All India Industrial Exhibition"],"_id":"DO0llYlypsg7dI4K"}
{"name":"Mysuru","slug":"mysuru","state":"Karnataka","tagline":"The Royal City of Grandeur and Dasara Splendor","description":"Mysuru is the cultural crown of Karnataka, renowned worldwide for its illuminated palace, Jamboo Savari elephant procession, and classical heritage.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1600100397608-f010f443b71a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":12.2958,"lng":76.6394},"culturalHighlights":["Mysuru Dasara Jamboo Savari","Chamundi Hill Chamundeshwari Rathotsava","Yuva Dasara Music Extravaganza"],"_id":"DuqFFrHWlXAKha6W"}
{"name":"Varanasi","slug":"varanasi","state":"Uttar Pradesh","tagline":"The Eternal Spiritual Capital of Moksha and Ganga Aarti","description":"The world oldest continuously inhabited city, where 84 ghats come alive with sacred chanting, evening Dev Deepawali diyas, and divine energy.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1561361513-2d000a50f0dc?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":25.3176,"lng":82.9739},"culturalHighlights":["Kashi Dev Deepawali","Ganga Mahotsav","Maha Shivaratri","Maha Kumbh Snan"],"_id":"GoUzFStOk4IJ65OS"}
{"name":"Mangaluru","slug":"mangaluru","state":"Karnataka","tagline":"Coastal Haven of Divine Daivaradhane and Kambala","description":"Mangaluru is celebrated for its sacred Bhuta Kola spirit worship, thunderous Kambala buffalo races, and vibrant coastal Dussehra.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":12.9141,"lng":74.856},"culturalHighlights":["Mangalore Dasara Tiger Dance (Pili Nalike)","Kadur Kambala Buffalo Races","Kadri Manjunatha Rathotsava"],"_id":"JJtJKMXbOtCMknFa"}
{"name":"Jaipur","slug":"jaipur","state":"Rajasthan","tagline":"The Pink City of Regal Forts, Folk Rhythms, and Fairs","description":"Jaipur is celebrated for its majestic heritage forts, Pushkar Camel Mela tours, Gangaur processions, and vibrant Kathputli puppetry.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1477587458883-47145ed94245?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":26.9124,"lng":75.7873},"culturalHighlights":["Teej Festival Royal Procession","Gangaur Festival","Jaipur Literature Festival"],"_id":"LjuOOZAESm9MbFos"}
{"name":"Mumbai","slug":"mumbai","state":"Maharashtra","tagline":"Vibrant Capital of Ganeshotsav and Kala Ghoda Arts","description":"Mumbai pulses with the grand devotional rhythms of Lalbaugcha Raja Ganpati Visarjan and the Kala Ghoda open-air street arts festival.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1570168007204-dfb528c6958f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":19.076,"lng":72.8777},"culturalHighlights":["Ganesh Chaturthi Lalbaugcha Raja","Kala Ghoda Arts Festival","Bandra Fair Mount Mary Feast"],"_id":"MtU64WyBA6Tb3sMm"}
{"name":"Mathura & Vrindavan","slug":"mathura-vrindavan","state":"Uttar Pradesh","tagline":"Land of Krishna Leela and Colorful Lathmar Holi","description":"The sacred birthplace of Lord Krishna where Braj culture, devotional Raas Leela, and flower-filled Phoolon Ki Holi enchant millions.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1583083527882-4bee9aba2eea?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":27.4924,"lng":77.6737},"culturalHighlights":["Braj Ki Lathmar Holi","Janmashtami Mahotsav","Radhashtami"],"_id":"OcAxNBRUBal9su0R"}
{"name":"Puri","slug":"puri","state":"Odisha","tagline":"The Abode of Lord Jagannath and Grand Rath Yatra","description":"Puri is holy Dham of Jagannath culture, world-famous for the grand chariot procession, golden beaches, and intricate temple architecture.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1629853689408-251f2f81e352?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":19.8135,"lng":85.8312},"culturalHighlights":["Puri Jagannath Rath Yatra","Chandan Yatra","Konark Sand Art Festival"],"_id":"Pdfw1MUO03YOMQIn"}
{"name":"Chennai","slug":"chennai","state":"Tamil Nadu","tagline":"The Soul of Carnatic Music and Dravidian Architecture","description":"Chennai is synonymous with the renowned December Margazhi music festival, majestic Kapaleeshwarar chariot festival, and classical Bharatanatyam.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":13.0827,"lng":80.2707},"culturalHighlights":["Margazhi Music & Dance Season","Mylapore Festival","Kapaleeshwarar Panguni Uthiram"],"_id":"S7LCym9hKQXXWQjf"}
{"name":"Kolkata","slug":"kolkata","state":"West Bengal","tagline":"City of Joy and UNESCO Intangible Cultural Heritage","description":"Kolkata comes alive with breathtaking artistic pandals during Durga Puja, accompanied by reverberating Dhak drums, Sindoor Khela, and Rabindra Sangeet.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1558431382-27e303142255?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":22.5726,"lng":88.3639},"culturalHighlights":["Durga Puja Pandal Hopping","Kolkata International Film Festival","Dover Lane Music Conference"],"_id":"UTiQboIKaC662XO0"}
{"name":"Ahmedabad","slug":"ahmedabad","state":"Gujarat","tagline":"World Heritage City of Navratri Garba and Kite Flying","description":"Ahmedabad pulses during nine nights of high-energy Garba dancing, colorful chaniya cholis, and the world International Kite Festival.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1609137144813-7d9921338f24?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":23.0225,"lng":72.5714},"culturalHighlights":["Navratri Mega Garba","International Kite Festival (Uttarayan)","Rann Utsav Tours"],"_id":"Y8v4bbJ0pmhnqABH"}
{"name":"Thrissur","slug":"thrissur","state":"Kerala","tagline":"The Cultural Capital of God Own Country and Grand Poorams","description":"Famed for Thrissur Pooram, the mother of all temple festivals featuring 30 caparisoned tuskers, dynamic percussion, and spectacular fireworks.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1602216056096-3b40cc0c9944?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":10.5276,"lng":76.2144},"culturalHighlights":["Thrissur Pooram","Ilanjithara Melam","Kudamattam Umbrella Exchange","Pulikali Tiger Dance"],"_id":"gyAPeEiGGSFw15sN"}
{"name":"Bengaluru","slug":"bengaluru","state":"Karnataka","tagline":"The Garden City of Timeless Traditions and Karaga Heritage","description":"Bengaluru harmoniously balances high-tech dynamism with ancient Pete festivals, historic temples, and iconic flowering avenues.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1596402184320-417e7178b2cd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":12.9716,"lng":77.5946},"culturalHighlights":["Bengaluru Karaga Shaktyotsava","Kadalekai Parishe Groundnut Fair","Chitra Santhe Art Fair","Basavanagudi Bull Temple celebrations"],"_id":"hCREa140Wd5I1SOa"}
{"name":"Guwahati","slug":"guwahati","state":"Assam","tagline":"Gateway to Northeast and Land of Kamakhya & Bihu Rhythms","description":"Flanked by the mighty Brahmaputra river, Guwahati celebrates the vibrant agricultural cycle with Rongali Bihu and the mystic Ambubachi Mela.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1616423640778-28d1b53229bd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":26.1445,"lng":91.7362},"culturalHighlights":["Rongali Bihu Spring Festival","Ambubachi Mela Kamakhya","Brahmaputra Beach Festival"],"_id":"lYNCuc9Xo5RpxTho"}
{"name":"Kohima","slug":"kohima","state":"Nagaland","tagline":"Land of the Great Hornbill and Vibrant Tribal Heritage","description":"Nestled in the lush hills of Northeast India, Kohima hosts the world-renowned Hornbill Festival bringing together 17 indigenous tribes.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":25.6751,"lng":94.1086},"culturalHighlights":["Hornbill Festival of Festivals","Naga Morung Architecture","Tribal War Dances"],"_id":"oB3PkTEoLC0Ep4Rw"}
{"name":"Madurai","slug":"madurai","state":"Tamil Nadu","tagline":"The Ancient Temple City of Goddess Meenakshi and Chithirai","description":"One of the oldest living cities in the world, dominated by the multi-tiered gopurams of Meenakshi Sundareswarar Temple and the roaring Jallikattu.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":9.9252,"lng":78.1198},"culturalHighlights":["Chithirai Thiruvizha (Divine Wedding)","Alanganallur Jallikattu","Float Festival"],"_id":"pDLcuJhHPaaCYLV3"}
{"name":"Kochi","slug":"kochi","state":"Kerala","tagline":"Queen of the Arabian Sea and Capital of Onam Carnival","description":"Kochi offers the vibrant Onam Athachamayam parade, mesmerising Kathakali performances, and the Kochi-Muziris Contemporary Biennale.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1602216056096-3b40cc0c9944?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":9.9312,"lng":76.2673},"culturalHighlights":["Athachamayam Thrippunithura","Cochin Carnival Fort Kochi","Kathakali & Theyyam Nights"],"_id":"u9Kofi1Kw03HKc0x"}
{"name":"Leh Ladakh","slug":"leh-ladakh","state":"Ladakh","tagline":"Roof of the World and Land of Mystic Buddhist Monasteries","description":"High-altitude mountain desert famous for colorful monastery festivals, Sacred Cham mask dances, and Tibetan Buddhist chants.","coverImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506197603052-3cc9c3a201bd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","coordinates":{"lat":34.1526,"lng":77.5771},"culturalHighlights":["Hemis Monastery Mask Dance","Ladakh Festival","Losar Tibetan New Year"],"_id":"xtvNbwZOiXn3cTuR"}
